.TH ZVM-ENV 1 "October 2026" "ZVM" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-env \- give the current shell its own Zig version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm env
.RB [ --shell
.IR shell ]
.RB [ --use-on-cd ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print shell code that gives the shell evaluating it a private Zig version.
.B zvm env
creates a per-shell link that points at the current global version (what
.I ~/.zvm/bin
points to), exports its path as
.BR ZVM_MULTISHELL_PATH ,
and prepends it to
.BR PATH ,
where it shadows
.IR ~/.zvm/bin .
If no global version is set, the link points at
.I ~/.zvm/bin
itself, so the shell follows the global version until it selects its own.
.PP
While
.B ZVM_MULTISHELL_PATH
names such a link,
.BR zvm-use (1)
repoints only that link; other shells and the global default are unchanged.
Use
.B zvm use --global
to change the default.
.PP
Per-shell links are stored in
.BR $ZVM_MULTISHELL_DIR ,
otherwise
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/zvm/multishells ,
otherwise
.I zvm/multishells
in the user cache directory
.RI ( ~/.cache
on Linux,
.I ~/Library/Caches
on macOS,
.I %LocalAppData%
on Windows).
Links older than a week whose shell has exited are removed by
.B zvm env
and
.BR zvm-clean (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --shell " shell"
Emit code for
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
or
.B powershell
.RB ( pwsh
is accepted).
Defaults to the basename of
.BR $SHELL ;
an unrecognised shell is an error.
.TP
.B --use-on-cd
Also install a hook that runs whenever the working directory changes.
It searches the new directory and then each parent for the nearest
.B //! zvm-lock:
line in
.I build.zig
or, failing that in the same directory,
.B .minimum_zig_version
in
.IR build.zig.zon ,
and switches this shell to that version.
If the version is not installed it prints a one-line hint and changes nothing;
if no version file is found it does nothing.
The hook never prompts and never changes the global version.
In bash the hook runs from
.B PROMPT_COMMAND
before the next prompt; zsh uses
.BR chpwd ,
fish a
.B PWD
variable handler, and PowerShell
.BR LocationChangedAction .
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
eval "$(zvm env --shell bash --use-on-cd)"     # ~/.bashrc
eval "$(zvm env --shell zsh --use-on-cd)"      # ~/.zshrc
zvm env --shell fish --use-on-cd | source      # config.fish
zvm env --shell powershell --use-on-cd | Out-String | Invoke-Expression
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-use (1),
.BR zvm-clean (1)
